  <ProbNet type="InfluenceDiagram">
    <Comment showWhenOpeningNetwork="true"><![CDATA[<html>
  <head>
    
  </head>
  <body>
    <p style="margin-top: 0">
      In this problem, if we order the test now, its result will be known 
      tomorrow. Therefore, the first decision, <i>Do test?</i>, reveals <i>Result 
      of test</i> but not immediately; when making the second decision, <i>Therapy 
      today</i>, the <i>Result of test</i> is still unknown. Similarly, <i>Symptom 
      tomorrow</i> is observed spontaneously, but only after the first two 
      decisions have been made. Therefore this problem cannot be represented 
      in a natural way using standard DANs.
    </p>
  </body>
</html>
